   "he": "הָיְתָה אַחַת מֵהֶם כּוּ׳. הָא תְּנֵינָא חֲדָא זִימְנָא: אֲחוֹתָהּ כְּשֶׁהִיא יְבִמְתָּהּ — אוֹ חוֹלֶצֶת אוֹ מִתְיַיבֶּמֶת!",
   "en": "§ The mishna stated: If «one of» the sisters «was» forbidden to one of the brothers due to a prohibition against forbidden relations, then he is prohibited from marrying her but permitted to marry her sister. The Gemara asks: «We» already «learned» this «on one occasion: When her sister,» who is a forbidden relative to the yavam, «is her yevama» as well, «she either performs ḥalitza or enters into levirate marriage.»"
  }
